{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure","id":74022,"title":"Adding \"magic\" to Adventure!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T18:55:52-08:00","id":74022,"title":"Adding \"magic\" to Adventure!","content":"OK, lets get a few things out of the way:<br /> 1) I am in no way involved with WW or Onyx Path.<br /> 2) No, Adventure! does not &quot;need&quot; a magic system.<br /> 3) &quot;Magic&quot; may indeed be anti-thematic to Adventure!<br /> 4) I am planning on designing one anyway.<br /> 5) Why? One word... Zombies!<br /> 6) What's the only thing better then killing Hitler? Getting to kill Zombie Hitler! (I tease. I just really love magic, and although Adventure is my favorite pulp action system, some times I just want to add cultists and stuff.)<br /> <br /> So, why am I bothering to post this here? Well, the way I see it. if I'm already going to be going thru all the effort of designing a magic system for Adventure, I might as well let other people enjoy it. I'm also interested in finding out what sorts of effects people think should be in a good pulp magic system.<br /> <br /> Now before I'm inundated by suggestions I have a few disclaimers:<br /> 1) No free form or point buy magic systems. I like Knacks and will be trying to fit the Mystics powers within the current mold as much as possible. (This does not mean that it can't be a unique take on Knacks, I'm just not wiling to abandon the system in it's entirety)<br /> 2) I would prefer that suggestions stay within the general power levels of the established knacks. (ie. No sinking of islands or blowing up of cities)<br /> 3) While some overlap is unavoidable, at no time should Eldritch Knacks overshadow the other types. (I call this the &quot;Don't piss in the other dudes cheerios&quot; rule)<br /> <br /> As you can tell, I'm thinking of calling them &quot;Mystics&quot;, and calling their powers &quot;Eldritch&quot; Knacks.<br /> <br /> So, please tell me, what sort of cool effects do you look for, and or want, in a pulp magic system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-17T20:12:16-08:00","id":74063,"title":"","content":"I do not agree with the idea of a magic system. But, with that being said, if you want to add it to your table, then I would be glad to help you.<br /> First off, to add in the feel of pulp, I would highly suggest that you make it a ritual. How many stories of the Phantom or The Shadow or even Indiana Jones were to stop someone from enacting some evil wicked ritual? Answer: a lot.<br /> A ritual can then be used to give certain Knacks/Attributes/What-have-you to a subject. Or else it can lay waste to larger areas. You can use rituals to bring forth zombies or to rain down plagues. It can also lead into stories of people acquiring the stuff they need or the elements for the ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T04:11:56-08:00","id":74191,"title":"","content":"I'd have to dig it up, but in the ancient era of the before-times there were some guidelines for converting the CWoD Sorcerer Revised system of hedge magic into Adventure! Sorcerers, under such a system, were basically considered an alternate, rarer form of Inspiration and the levels of Paths were bought like Knacks. If you'd like I can see if I still have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T07:40:43-08:00","id":74256,"title":"","content":"I would probably use the Super-Science rules as a base; rather than just throwing spells around, you 'build' them over time using rare ingredients and strange events, and then they mimic a Knack when they are cast. <br /> <br /> Psionic knacks already act a lot like spells half the time, too, so a Psionic player with the ability to create ritual spells pretty much has everything covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T07:49:42-08:00","id":74259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74063#post74063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not agree with the idea of a magic system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this is going to sound funny, but I totally agree with you. I would never include magic of any sort into the default Adventure Setting. However there are times that I want to use Adventure for other pulp settings or stories, and for those times I would really like some sort of magic system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74063#post74063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, with that being said, if you want to add it to your table, then I would be glad to help you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74063#post74063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First off, to add in the feel of pulp, I would highly suggest that you make it a ritual. How many stories of the Phantom or The Shadow or even Indiana Jones were to stop someone from enacting some evil wicked ritual? Answer: a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually already given this some thought, and I think that the rules for Innovative Super-Science on pg 182 of the Adventure Rulebook could cover any rituals and high powered effects that players would be rushing all over the globe to stop. This would also allow them to give Knacks to others as you suggested, but I feel that they need/should have unique Knacks of their own. As a bonus, this also lends to those stories where you have to track down the ritual ingredients and such.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T07:52:18-08:00","id":74262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74191#post74191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to dig it up, but in the ancient era of the before-times there were some guidelines for converting the CWoD Sorcerer Revised system of hedge magic into Adventure! Sorcerers, under such a system, were basically considered an alternate, rarer form of Inspiration and the levels of Paths were bought like Knacks. If you'd like I can see if I still have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see that. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T07:58:13-08:00","id":74267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74256#post74256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would probably use the Super-Science rules as a base; rather than just throwing spells around, you 'build' them over time using rare ingredients and strange events, and then they mimic a Knack when they are cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>For big ritual effects I totally agree with you. However, not all effects need to be ritual in nature and I feel that for certain settings and games a &quot;quicker&quot; system is needed. (at least for lesser effects)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrivYeti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74256#post74256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Psionic knacks already act a lot like spells half the time, too, so a Psionic player with the ability to create ritual spells pretty much has everything covered.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can see where you are coming from, and I mostly agree with you. I still feel that there is enough room to play with for another type of inspired. One of the things that I will be closely looking at is the relationship between Mystics and the other types of inspired to make sure that I'm not stepping on the others areas of expertise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T09:59:10-08:00","id":74345,"title":"","content":"Here we go. I was able to find these without having to dig back through my old files for local copies.<br /> <br /> First, a disclaimer: These guidelines assume you actually have a copy of Sorcerer Revised. They don't reproduce the rules from that system, they just explain how to use one in the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://digital.raven.tripod.com/rp/mystics.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the difficulty conversion chart (the link's dead on the original page) can be found here: <a href=\"http://web.archive.org/web/20020612152615/http://www.mindspring.com/~brucebaugh/trinity/charts.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://web.archive.org/web/200206121...ty/charts.html</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":171,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","user":"MythicFox","date":".  Fixed the formatting. Finally. 02-21-2014, 03:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:01:48-08:00","id":74348,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the lack of proper line breaks, posting from my phone at the moment. I'll have to fix it later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T10:08:18-08:00","id":74355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74348#post74348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here we go. I was able to find these without having to dig back through my old files for local copies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for going thru all the trouble to find this. I haven't had time to look it over, so I'm not sure how much of this I'll be able to use, but I appreciate the effort that you went thru to get this for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74348#post74348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, a disclaimer: These guidelines assume you actually have a copy of Sorcerer Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do. Somewhere... I think I also have the PDF from DTRPG if nothing else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/74022-adding-magic-to-adventure?p=74348#post74348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for the lack of proper line breaks, posting from my phone at the moment. I'll have to fix it later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't worry about it. I have to post from my phone all of the time. It happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T12:39:50-08:00","id":76498,"title":"","content":"I once devised a setting inspired by, but distinct from, the Trinity Universe that had three \u201cexotic abilities\u201d types rather than two<sup>*</sup>: <i>superhumans</i> specialized in exotic abilities of the body; <i>psychics</i> specialized in exotic abilities of the mind; and <i>mystics</i> specialized in exotic abilities of the soul.<sup>\u2020</sup> There <i>was</i> overlap, mind you: psychokinetics existed, as did superhumans with powers that could influence minds; but the superhuman elementals were better at manipulating fire than the psychic pyrokinetics were, and the psychic telepaths were better at messing with minds than the superhuman \u201cinterfacers\u201d were. <br /> <br /> I gave each type two areas of expertise: superhumans got self-empowerment (ranging from augmenting traits to varying degrees of shapeshifting) and elementalism (controlling elements of the environment around them); psychics got telepathy (reading and influencing minds) and ESP (remote sensing, aura sight, etc.); and mystics got ensorcelment (summoning, binding, and warding of spirits) and enchantment (blessings, curses, geases, and fortune telling). <br /> <hr /><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">* I\u2019m in the camp that classifies daredevils as talented baselines rather than a third \u201cempowered\u201d type; but that\u2019s a debate for another time and place.</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">\u2020 Also of note is that this variant was primarily supernatural rather than superscience: e.g., the \u201csuperhumans\u201d were conceived as \u201cchi masters\u201d.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:16:18-08:00","id":76625,"title":"","content":"All that said: magicians in <b>Adventure!</b>? I\u2019d handle them as Inspired characters with access to a selection of Mystic Knacks; and I\u2019d use the Thaumaturgy Merits from <b>World of Darkness: Second Sight</b> as inspiration for said Knacks. Not necessarily a direct translation, mind you; but I figure that for the most part, the sorts of things that Thaumaturgy Merits let you do should be the sorts of things that Mystic Knacks ought to let you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-22T08:04:30-08:00","id":77069,"title":"","content":"Aside from the really excellent stuff in Second Sight, I think you could reskin a lot of existing Knacks for both Stalwarts and Mesmerists pretty well I think, especially if you use Super Science as the model for rituals. For instance, Body of Bronze seems pretty ripe for a mystic origin with some suitable alteration. <br /> <br /> People could even argue about the source of it, so a lot of &quot;magic&quot; could be BS, which might be a neat campaign concept with the PCs trying to be debunkers or facing off against debunkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2173-jvv","name":"JVV","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T09:11:20-08:00","id":81616,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve done the magic-as-misunderstood-psionics thing before, and it can be interesting. Likewise with magic-as-misunderstood-superscience. I\u2019d prefer, though, that magic be something that feels like its own thing, not merely a reskinning of an existing set. A magician should be able to do things that a mesmerist or stalwart can\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:20:54-08:00","id":81645,"title":"","content":"So, I've been testing your suggestions with my group, and I've come to a conclusion. While re-skinning someone elses work works, it's fairly cludgy and not quite as well intigrated as we'd like it to be. Therefore I'm asking you, what sort of effects should Mystics have to keep them distinct and cool when compared to the other types of Inspired?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-28T10:47:48-08:00","id":81664,"title":"","content":"First, a bit about the rules: Mystic Knacks should all take time (i.e., extended actions) and probably some material components, usually of a sort that gets consumed by the ritual. The Reflective Facet should be big where magicians are concerned, even moreso than for mesmerists. Some knacks may impose additional requirements. I\u2019d also have them cost a point of Inspiration each, like Psychic Knacks. <br /> <br /> <b>Second Sight</b> has 29 Thaumaturge Merits, four of which don\u2019t so much represent rituals as resources (Dream, Familiar, Library, Magical Nexus). Of the rest, there are some interdependencies; but for the most part, you can buy the Merits in any order you wish. There\u2019s External Alchemy (i.e., transmuting substances), various health-related Merits (Internal Alchemy that lets you boost your own traits, Longevity which combats aging, and Healing), some spirit-related Merits (Evocation, Invocation, and Sacrifice), some altered-consciousness Merits (Visionary Trances, plus Dream Travel, Psychic Projection, and See Spirits), some defensive Merits (Counterspell and Warding), some knowledge-acquisition Merits (Communion, Divination, Scrying, Second Sight, See Auras), some fate-manipulation Merits (Luck Magic, plus Curse of Ill Fortune and Favorable Fortune), and some miscellaneous Merits (Enchantment which influences emotions, Geomancy a.k.a. Feng Shui, Soul Jar, and Weather Control). As I said a few posts back, you could do worse than to use this as inspiration for what Mystic Knacks ought to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Oh: <b>Second Sight</b> also has a selection of Psychic Merits, which should be compared to the Psychic Knacks to see if there are any holes that should be filled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2014, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}